35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"I found that in fixed-rate houses, people just leave the heat on. It feels much more relaxed.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The bills swing wildly. February was 29k, August 9k. A flat rate would be a disaster for me.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,The template is a nightmare. Keying in every invoice takes hours. I don't want to do that.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,The monitor shows one room uses four times more than another. The current split is definitely unfair.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Misaki,,The payment log shows delays happen when people question the amount. The cooler notice shows we avoid conflict by suffering.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi That confirms it. The north rooms need heat, the south don't. We need a way to account for that.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,@Mio A seasonal fixed rate might work if the winter figure is high enough. But the upfront cost for meters is 170k yen.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,@Ryuji 170k is a lot. And the monthly settle at the other house took 40 minutes. I don't have that time.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin The 40 minutes is for logging. If we use a template, it might be faster, but the trial run was bad.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Rin The delays are because the amounts change. If we fix the amount, the conflict might stop.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,I really like the idea of a seasonal fixed rate. It removes the anxiety of checking the meter.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"I am hesitant. The variance is too high. If we fix the rate, someone will always be overpaying in summer.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I am worried about the admin. If we go with meters, who does the 40 minutes of logging?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,The data supports per-room metering. It is the only way to be fair given the usage difference.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Misaki,,I think the social damage is the biggest issue. A fixed rate might reduce the arguments about the amount.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
